[Music]  it's often said that it's easier to be  something if you can see if you could  imagine yourself in that position and so  role models have always played an  important role in that role models have  that role I have a slightly contrary and  view of role models where if you need  someone who looks exactly like you to do  something you want to do but no one has  done it before you then you would never  do anything new so for me in my life I  assembled my role models ala carte so I  found the scientist who had a total  command of cosmology in the universe and  I said I want to one day I want to be  that smart and I want to know that much  oh there was an educator who who taught  with such enthusiasm and humor and with  such a sense of caring I said if I'm in  it ever an educator that's the kind of  educator I want to be and and my parents  they they they were active in the civil  rights movement and just their general  life's concern for other people people  less fortunate than you are the concern  for Humanity I said if I ever want to  what kind of a person should I be I'd  like that  model alright so I pieced it all  together and I said this is this that's  my role model this sort of frankenstein  assembly of parts and in that way if  there's someone who struggled through  whatever bias or resistance that's out  there you talk to them about their  struggles whether or not this struggle  happened to be in the field that you're  interested in entering your struggles  have a way of manifesting similarly no  matter the field so so in terms of  gender parity in various fields that do  not yet show it I think if you want to  go someplace where others have never  been before  talk to people who have struggled  whether or not they're in the field  you're aiming for they will have stories  that you can use and tap in fully  exploit in the service of your ambitions  and don't let the absence of someone who  looks just like you  be the reason why you don't become what  you've always dreamt of being  [Music]

